response:
 The equation $|5x - 1| = |3x + 2|$ can be split into two cases: $5x - 1 = 3x + 2$ and $5x - 1 = -(3x + 2)$. Solving the first case: \[
5x - 1 = 3x + 2 \implies 5x - 3x = 2 + 1 \implies 2x = 3 \implies x = \frac{3}{2}
\] Solving the second case: \[
5x - 1 = -(3x + 2) \implies 5x - 1 = -3x - 2 \implies 5x + 3x = -2 + 1 \implies 8x = -1 \implies x = -\frac{1}{8}
\] The smallest value of $x$ is $-\frac{1}{8}$. </think> <answer> $-\frac{1}{8}$ </answer>

